sequenceDiagram
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · started by proof:run
  %% kind: proof.command
  autonumber
  participant GW as Gateway
  participant SW as Swamp
  participant CP as Proof copy
  GW->>SW: Start one shard<br/>operation-proof-run-copy
  %%> Admission recorded one group and its copy with its assigned parts (a batch and its case ids) and the expected expanded case ids, and the run budget of the shard from its parts: 600 s, 180 s a part that is not read-only and the measured case seconds, times 1.5, rounded up to five minutes, at most two hours. The run starts only once its copy is active. Each development deploy step's command goes to its own vault key at the start.
  SW->>CP: Bring in the commit
  %%> One Ansible phase on the copy's Node fetches the commit by its SHA from the public Orbit repository, as `agent`, the workspace's owner (ADR 0268), and checks it out detached. A fetch that fails or takes more than 60 seconds fails the run; nothing retries.
  SW->>CP: Read the steps to skip
  SW->>CP: Run dev deploy steps
  %%> Each development deploy step whose inputs changed since the seed, from its vault copy, as a deployment runs it.
  SW->>CP: Read the workspace commit
  SW->>SW: Check the workspace commit
  %%> A mismatch fails before cases and records expected and found commits.
  loop assigned batches, one at a time
    SW->>CP: Prove assigned batches
    %%> Each batch is one proof-fleet-verify child: the reset of the copy's inner fleet to base, the batch setup and its cases, with every verdict line in the output artifact. A copy replays no flagged case on the merge base (`fails_on_base: true`) until the replay is ported to copies.
    CP-->>SW: Batch verdicts
    SW-->>GW: Batch run ended
    %%> The Gateway reads each ended batch run with the parent's reconcile and records its full report artifact on the shard, once.
  end
  SW->>CP: Remove the run folder
  SW->>SW: Report<br/>full verdict artifact
  %%> Prefix each line with its command, file and batch. The fixed capture reads the full artifact rather than the 4 KiB history summary.
  SW-->>GW: Native terminal result
  GW->>GW: Record all expected cases
  %%> Preserve native interrupted status and record outcome interrupted; it never passes, even with all passed rows. Otherwise failed, missing, duplicate or unassigned verdicts fail the shard. Keep recorded batch reports even if interruption prevents the final report. Keep completed case verdicts and synthesize missing cases as unrun. The parent closes one merged report after all shards end.
  %%> A shard that reaches its run budget is timed out: it keeps the recorded verdicts of the batches that ended, and only the cases of the other batches are unrun.
  GW->>GW: Cancel the group
  %%> Every end of the run, however it ends, cancels its group with discard, which destroys the copy.
